rection from the point $(0,3)$ to the point $(-2,0).$" 13194139535501 true] [17592186352345 1113 #uuid "0814c9bc-122f-53c2-a756-b81f1b80f4de" 13194139535501 true] [17592186352345 1145 "Since $C$ is an ellipse centered at $O$ with horizontal and vertical semiaxes of $2$ and $3,$ respectively, it can be parametrized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,t\\in [\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & ={x}^{′}(t)\\,i+{y}^{′}(t)\\,j=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}(x-y)\\,dx+(x+y)\\,dy & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(x-y)\\,\\frac{dx}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t+(x+y)\\,\\frac{dy}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }((x-y)\\,\\frac{dx}{\\text{d}t}+(x+y)\\,\\frac{dy}{\\text{d}t})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\cdot 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+6{sin}^{2}⁡t+6{cos}^{2}⁡t+9\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+6\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t+6\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+6t]}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =[(-\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi )+6\\pi )-(-\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+3\\pi )] \\\\  & =(-\\frac{5}{4}+6\\pi )-(\\frac{5}{4}+3\\pi ) \\\\  & =3\\pi -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\pi -5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535501 true] [17592186352346 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352347 13194139535501 true] [17592186352346 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352348 13194139535501 true] [17592186352346 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352349 13194139535501 true] [17592186352346 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352350 13194139535501 true] [17592186352346 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352351 13194139535501 true] [17592186352346 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535501 true] [17592186352346 1041 "selection" 13194139535501 true] [17592186352346 1104 #edb/ref 17592186352351 13194139535501 true] [17592186352346 1110 #uuid "63838486-62db-561a-b0a0-898d48bc4de6" 13194139535501 true] [17592186352347 1034 "\\frac{12\\pi -5}{4}" 13194139535501 true] [17592186352347 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535501 true] [17592186352347 1111 #uuid "9ac7a92e-45db-5339-954a-3d12f0af502b" 13194139535501 true] [17592186352348 1034 "\\frac{5\\pi +1}{4}" 13194139535501 true] [17592186352348 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535501 true] [17592186352348 1111 #uuid "7ce5dc3a-e973-568d-84b3-65b310c6a3de" 13194139535501 true] [17592186352349 1034 "3\\pi " 13194139535501 true] [17592186352349 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535501 true] [17592186352349 1111 #uuid "5834f9df-e912-5850-8c34-b424f767e97e" 13194139535501 true] [17592186352350 1034 "6\\pi " 13194139535501 true] [17592186352350 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535501 true] [17592186352350 1111 #uuid "63102b81-f990-580b-9d83-074239c7f80d" 13194139535501 true] [17592186352351 1034 "\\frac{6\\pi -5}{2}" 13194139535501 true] [17592186352351 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535501 true] [17592186352351 1111 #uuid "5fc63b1a-0f79-5065-ab5a-4326d53873c5" 13194139535501 true] [17592186352352 1017 #edb/ref 17592186352353 13194139535501 true] [17592186352352 1089 "q-81098" 13194139535501 true] [17592186352352 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535501 true] [17592186352352 1100 "If the path $C$ is a part of the parabola $y={x}^{2}-x$ traversed from the point $A(0,0)$ to point $B(2,2),$ then ${\\int }_{C}2xy\\,dx+x\\,dy=$" 13194139535501 true] [17592186352352 1113 #uuid "f6bed643-ce3e-507d-aa72-c9eaa603d013" 13194139535501 true] [17592186352352 1145 "Notice that our curve is given by the explicit Cartesian equation $y={x}^{2}-x.$ As a result, we obtain the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t)=x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j=t\\,i+({t}^{2}-t)\\,j,\\,t\\in [0,2]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j=i+(2t-1)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}2xy\\,dx+x\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2xy\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t+x\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(2xy\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2t({t}^{2}-t)\\cdot 1+t(2t-1)\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2{t}^{3}-t\\,dt \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{t}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{{2}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2}]-[0] \\\\  & =8-2 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535501 true] [17592186352353 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352354 13194139535501 true] [17592186352353 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352355 13194139535501 true] [17592186352353 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352356 13194139535501 true] [17592186352353 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352357 13194139535501 true] [17592186352353 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352358 13194139535501 true] [17592186352353 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535501 true] [17592186352353 1041 "selection" 13194139535501 true] [17592186352353 1104 #edb/ref 17592186352358 13194139535501 true] [17592186352353 1110 #uuid "4251c9c6-fdf9-5223-88ef-f8a83ccbe5e9" 13194139535501 true] [17592186352354 1034 "12" 13194139535501 true] [17592186352354 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535501 true] [17592186352354 1111 #uuid "ce41c1b2-83ff-599a-bbd5-92d83d9143de" 13194139535501 true] [17592186352355 1034 "9" 13194139535501 true] [17592186352355 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535501 true] [17592186352355 1111 #uuid "dd1cc6dd-9d67